<title>FRANCE: Thomson-CSF price speculative - Lagardere.</title>
<headline>Thomson-CSF price speculative - Lagardere.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The price of Thomson-CSF shares, up 12 percent since the start of the year, reflects speculation, said Philippe Camus, managing director of Lagardere, which is bidding for Thomson-CSF.</p>
<p>&quot;I frankly feel the price is speculative,&quot; he told reporters at a presentation on Wednesday of Lagardere's 1996 results.</p>
<p>The French state owns 58 percent of Thomson-CSF, whose privatisation is under way, and the rest is held by minorities.</p>
<p>During the failed effort last year to privatise Thomson, Lagardere proposed to buy out the minorities for 156 francs per share.</p>
<p>Thomson-CSF shares closed at 188.50 francs on Wednesday, up 1.95 percent.</p>
<p>Lagardere said last Friday that it was submitting a bid for Thomson-CSF as part of the relaunched privatisation of the defence electronics firm.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
